-- title:
--   Scaled Gauss order attained at the normal form
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a discrete valuation domain that is adically complete for its maximal ideal, let $\varpi \in W$ be irreducible, and let $e \ge 1$ and $q \ge 1$ be natural numbers. Consider the crossing model $R = W[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1 - \varpi^{e})$, the quotient of the two-variable power series ring `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) W` by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - C(\varpi^{e})$, and let $x \in R$. Let $(a,b)$ be a pair of one-variable power series over $W$ with $b$ of zero constant term, and suppose that the class of $\mathrm{inU}(a) + \mathrm{inV}(b)$ in $R$ is $x$, where $\mathrm{inU}(a)$ has coefficient $a_{d_0}$ at the multi-index $d$ when $d_1 = 0$ and $0$ otherwise, and $\mathrm{inV}(b)$ has coefficient $b_{d_1}$ when $d_0 = 0$ and $0$ otherwise. Let $p \le qe$. Measure coefficients by $w \mapsto q \cdot \mathrm{addVal}_W(w) \in \mathbb{N}\cup\{\infty\}$. Then the supremum, over all lifts $F \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ of $x$, of $\inf_{d} \bigl(q\,\mathrm{addVal}_W(\mathrm{coeff}_d F) + d_0 p + d_1 (qe - p)\bigr)$ equals the value of that infimum at the single lift $\mathrm{inU}(a) + \mathrm{inV}(b)$; that is, the scaled Gauss order of $x$ at index $p$ is computed on the normal form, the infimum there running effectively over the two coordinate axes $q\,v(a_i) + ip$ and $q\,v(b_j) + j(qe-p)$.
--
--   This is the computation lemma for the Gauss order on the width-$e$ crossing model, in the scaled form in which the index $p \le qe$ stands for the rational depth $p/q$ on the annulus $0 \le v(U) \le e$: the supremum over lifts defining the Gauss order is attained at the normal-form lift $a(U) + b(V)$. It is used in the place-specialisation development, in the lemmas on prolongation tuples that identify slope drops and Gauss orders of coordinates along a chain of annuli.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_gaussOrder_scaled_eq_repGaussOrder_normalForm.lean

